SUMMARY:HMEI: Faculty Seminar "The search for materials to revive soil he
 alth and scavenge greenhouse gases" by Satish Myneni
DESCRIPTION:The High Meadows Environmental Institute (HMEI) will host a s
 eminar by Satish Myneni\, professor of Geosciences\, on Tuesday\, Dec. 1
 . Myneni is the final speaker in the Fall 2026 HMEI Faculty Seminar Seri
 es. Centuries of farming\, grazing and erosion have depleted essential m
 inerals and nutrients from topsoils\, threatening global crop yields. Th
 e presentation outlines how to revive soil health\, and regenerate soil 
 minerals using optimum earth materials\, while also helping capture the 
 atmospheric CO2 and lowering other greenhouse gas emissions. This semina
 r is free and open to the public. Lunch wi\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/hmei-faculty-seminar-search-materials-revive-soil-health-and-s
 cavenge-greenhouse-gases
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/hmei-faculty-seminar-search-mat
 erials-revive-soil-health-and-scavenge-greenhouse-gases
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
