SUMMARY:Friends of PUL Small Talk: "A Librarian's War" with Molly Guptill
  Manning
DESCRIPTION:Molly Guptill Manning returns to the Friends on Thursday\, De
 cember 3 with a new tale about Ray Trautman\, the librarian behind the 
 “Armed Services Editions” that brought nearly half a billion wallet-
 sized paperbacks and miniature magazines to American troops during World
  War II. Trautman fought relentlessly for this idea that he believed wou
 ld inspire troops and boost morale\, going against military leaders at t
 he time. In the decades after the war\, Trautman focused on promoting li
 teracy and access to books across the country. New York Times bestsellin
 g author\, professor\, and lawyer Manning argu\nhttps://www.princeton.ed
 u/events/2026/friends-pul-small-talk-librarians-war-molly-guptill-mannin
 g
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/friends-pul-small-talk-libraria
 ns-war-molly-guptill-manning
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
