SUMMARY:Musicology Colloquium with Matthew Gelbart
DESCRIPTION:The Musicology Colloquium presents a talk by Matthew Gelbart.
 AbstractWhether to uphold it or attack it\, commentators have often spok
 en of “the Western canon” of music. Others have stressed the existen
 ce of “multiple canons” simultaneously. Both of these approaches mak
 e sense\, but neither can stand on its own. I start from the idea that s
 haping and enforcing any canon is a dynamic exercise in authority and co
 mmunity-building storytelling\; and all communities\, from the most loca
 l to those imagined at international scale\, exist in a broad framework 
 of power and discourse. Dvořák reception provide\nhttps://www.princeto
 n.edu/events/2026/musicology-colloquium-matthew-gelbart
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/musicology-colloquium-matthew-g
 elbart
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
