SUMMARY:Common or Garden Cosmopolitics
DESCRIPTION:This talk draws on work in progress on the burgeoning theme-p
 ark-like gardens\, parks\, and public spaces in contemporary India whose
  figuration of what we call “nature” returns us to basic questions a
 bout what such figuration can mean and do. At these sites\, a range of p
 ost-Enlightenment and post-Romantic ideas\, including global discourses 
 of ecology or environmentalism\, encounter other vernacular logics of pr
 esenting and representing nature. Engaging Lorraine Daston’s insights 
 into nature’s recalcitrant links with morality\, I describe how\, in s
 uch spaces\, logics of cosmic efficacy and social o\nhttps://www.princet
 on.edu/events/2026/common-or-garden-cosmopolitics
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/common-or-garden-cosmopolitics
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
