SUMMARY:Fieldwork on Fire: What you don't know about the fires in Indones
 ia threatening orangutans with rapid extinction
DESCRIPTION:Are you curious about what it’s like to be Jane Goodall or 
 Birute Galdikas? The life of a primatologist is full of adventure\, but 
 for those of us who study orangutans and other Indonesian primates\, the
  adventure becomes overwhelming when El Nino events exacerbate near-annu
 al fires in the dry season. When this happens\, as it is now\, the field
 workers\, researchers\, and local communities become the fire fighters -
  building hydrants in the forest\, hosing down fires in the trees above 
 and peat underground. Right now\, more than 34\,000 fires in Indonesia h
 ave burned over 800\,000 hectares of forest spa\nhttps://www.princeton.e
 du/events/2026/fieldwork-fire-what-you-dont-know-about-fires-indonesia-t
 hreatening-orangutans-rapid
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/fieldwork-fire-what-you-dont-kn
 ow-about-fires-indonesia-threatening-orangutans-rapid
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
