SUMMARY:Betrayal by Harold Pinter
DESCRIPTION:Betrayal\, one of Harold Pinter’s most acclaimed works\, de
 buted in 1978. The play follows three characters: Robert\, Emma\, Robert
 ’s wife\, and Jerry\, Robert’s university friend and Emma’s clande
 stine lover. Unfolding in reverse chronological order over the span of n
 early a decade\, the action starts at the end of Emma and Robert’s mar
 riage in 1977 and traces back to the beginning of Emma and Jerry’s aff
 air in 1968. Immersive staging invites audiences to watch alongside the 
 characters and witness acts of deceit\, unfulfilled dreams\, and all-con
 suming passion.Featuring Joe McLean '27\, with direction \nhttps://www.p
 rinceton.edu/events/2026/betrayal-harold-pinter-0
